\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:6:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'ls -ld /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/10 /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'ls -ld /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/10 /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"drwxrwxr-x+ 5 lixinyu lixinyu 4096 Jun 19 08:35 /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/10\\ndrwxrwxr-x+ 2 xd      xd      4096 May 26 23:32 /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:16:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10 -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:17:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10 -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/des.md\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/ids.txt\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/prompt.md\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:19:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/10/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"88e364bc\\\" lines=\\\"102-115\\\">\\n<description>\\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\\n\\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"6cbe9eb8\\\" lines=\\\"79-94\\\">\\n<description>\\nRebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\\n- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\\n- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\\n\\nRule\\n- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\\n- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\\n- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"230f2e48\\\" lines=\\\"19-38\\\">\\n<description>\\nFold each straight red rod at its black marker, leaving the gray-anchored side fixed.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- Each foreground object is a straight horizontal or vertical 4-connected rod.\\n- Each rod contains many pixels of one line color, one endpoint marker, and one\\n  interior control marker.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For every rod, keep the segment from the endpoint marker through the control\\n  marker unchanged.\\n- Move the line-color tail on the far side of the control marker to a\\n  perpendicular ray starting next to that marker.\\n- Choose the perpendicular direction with more space to the grid edge.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The endpoint marker identifies the fixed side of the rod, while the control\\n  marker is the hinge; the tail folds into the larger open half-plane.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"b7256dcd\\\" lines=\\\"18-32\\\">\\n<description>\\nTransfer each colored marker to its adjacent neutral mask component, then erase the markers.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The background is the most common color.\\n- The neutral mask color is the unique most frequent foreground color.\\n- Other foreground colors are marker pixels that may touch neutral 4-connected mask components.\\nRule\\n- Remove every marker pixel by recoloring it to the background.\\n- For each 4-connected neutral mask component, find marker colors touching it by edge adjacency.\\n- If a component touches one marker color, recolor the whole neutral component to that marker color.\\n- If a component touches no marker color, leave it neutral.\\nKey insight\\n- Marker pixels label neighboring neutral regions but are not part of the final colored objects.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"458e3a53\\\" lines=\\\"19-32\\\">\\n<description>\\nExtract the compact table of solid cells hidden inside a separator lattice.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has full-width and full-height bars of one separator color, dividing it into rectangular cells.\\n- Most cells contain a repeating multicolor pattern, while a contiguous rectangle of cells is solid monochrome.\\n\\nRule\\n- Split the input into lattice cells using the full separator rows and columns.\\n- Keep the cells whose full interior is one color, crop to their occupied rectangle, and output those colors.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The periodic pattern is noise; only completely solid lattice cells encode the reduced output grid.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"db695cfb\\\" lines=\\\"8-19\\\">\\n<description>\\nConnect same-color diagonal pixel pairs, then emit perpendicular rays from differently-colored pixels on those diagonals.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. Line color (e.g. blue) has pixel pairs aligned on shared diagonals. Trigger color (e.g. magenta) pixels sit along those diagonals.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Draw diagonal lines connecting each pair of same-color aligned pixels.\\n- Where the diagonal crosses a trigger pixel, emit perpendicular diagonal rays (in the trigger's color) extending to the grid boundary.\\n\\nKey insight: Trigger pixels act as beam-splitters — the perpendicular rays rotate 90° from the connecting diagonal's orientation.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"25c199f5\\\" lines=\\\"30-44\\\">\\n<description>\\nPack the non-background rows from three separated panels into one panel, scanning panels right-to-left.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A rectangular grid contains three equal-size panels separated by two full-height divider columns.\\n- The background is the dominant color; divider pixels use a color that appears only in the divider columns.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Read panels from right to left, and within each panel read rows from top to bottom.\\n- Keep each row that contains any non-background pixel, discarding all-background rows.\\n- Place the kept rows at the bottom of a single panel-shaped output, padding above with background rows.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The task is row packing: the divider columns mark independent panels, and only the occupied rows are moved.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"99caaf76\\\" lines=\\\"56-75\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color\\n  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.\\n- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly\\n  one side of the cross.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object\\n  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.\\n- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.\\n- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.\\n\\nKey insight:\\nThe marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,\\nand only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"db0c5428\\\" lines=\\\"32-51\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand a 3x3 block motif into a 5x5 block motif around its missing center.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- Teal background surrounds one 9x9 foreground motif.\\n- The motif is a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks; the middle block is empty teal.\\n- Colored pixels immediately around the empty middle block encode the border\\n  of the missing center block.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Keep the original 9x9 motif in place.\\n- Copy each of the eight surrounding 3x3 blocks to the opposite outer slot\\n  of the implied 5x5 block grid, without rotating it.\\n- Fill the center block from the eight pixels around the hole; its center is\\n  the motif's majority foreground color.\\n\\nKey insight: The visible 9x9 motif is the middle of a larger periodic\\nblock-level pattern, and the empty center is reconstructed from its immediate\\ninner boundary.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"e3721c99\\\" lines=\\\"69-83\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.\\n- Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,\\n  each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.\\n- For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).\\n- Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.\\n\\nKey insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"8698868d\\\" lines=\\\"9-23\\\">\\n<description>\\nMatch sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.\\n- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).\\n\\nRule:\\n- Frames form a regular grid; some may be bg-colored (invisible).\\n- Count connected hole regions inside each frame's interior and each sprite.\\n- Pair each frame with the sprite sharing the same hole count.\\n- Place the matched sprite inside the frame border; recolor sprite holes to the frame's color.\\n\\nKey insight: The matching key is the number of connected hole components, not hole area or color.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"0934a4d8\\\" lines=\\\"75-90\\\">\\n<description>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_083548_seed262781723_gpt54_high/seed262781723__10__codegen_prompts__1.log:21:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"if [ -f /home/lixinyu/s